Hi guys,

I am currently building my online resume, using shiny (https://nhatbui.shinyapps.io/NEW_SHINY_RESUME/) . The way I structure my site is  I created separate HTML files for each tabs and let shiny load it the HTML when user click on the tab. I figure since html files are light so shiny would not take too much time to render.

It runs very well locally. But, when I uploaded my site onto shiny server, some the HTML files load at first ( you guys can click onto different tabs and see it). However, after a couple of clicks , shiny stop loading the files. Is there other way I can include html files so shiny can load them quick?

The GitHub for this project is : https://github.com/minhnhat992/NEW_SHINY_RESUME

Below is  a portion of the codes when I used to load HTML :

  ----- ui.R -----

shinyUI(fluidPage(
  titlePanel("Uploading Files"),
  mainPanel(
    htmlOutput("inc")
  )
))

#  ----- server.R -----

shinyServer(function(input, output) {
  getPage<-function() {
      return(includeHTML("include.html"))
  }
  output$inc<-renderUI({getPage()})
})
That is to load 1 HTML file and I have around 9 or 10 lines of  code like this

Thank you

